course: dictionary
lesson: 4441
title: A handshake in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A handshake is when two people take each other's right hand and shake it. Break the word into two parts, hand and shake, and you can already picture what it means.
explain: People shake hands to say hello, goodbye, well done, or to agree. «A firm handshake» is a strong, friendly grip, the kind a grown-up might expect when you meet them.
explain: Context tells you which reason it is. At the end of a game, «shake hands» means good game. When two people agree a deal, the handshake shows they have both said yes. Ask yourself: what is the handshake doing in this sentence?
explain: Maths can use the word too. «With 4 children there are 6» handshakes, because each pair of people shakes hands only once. Count pairs, not hands, and the answer makes sense.
fact: A handshake is when two people take each other's right hand and shake it.
fact: «Handshake» is a noun: one handshake, or two or more handshakes.
fact: A «firm friendly handshake» shows respect when you meet someone.
fact: At the end of a sports game, the handshake shows respect for the game and the other team, win or lose.
fact: In a maths problem, each pair of people shakes hands once, so 8 children make 28 handshakes.
exercise: In a group of 4 children, each pair shakes hands once. How many handshakes are there? | 8 | 3 | 12 | *6
exercise: Ayesha says «a firm handshake» means a limp, weak one. What is a firm handshake? | *A strong, friendly grip | A soft, floppy grip | A wave from far away | A handshake done with your left hand
exercise: «Shake hands» at the end of a game means what? | Shout at the other team | *Good game, well played | Start the match again | Please leave the pitch
test: Why do people shake hands? | *To say hello, goodbye, well done, or to agree | To sing a song | To ring a bell | To make a cake
test: In «Inside jokes and secret handshakes help friends feel close», what do secret handshakes do? | Show that a teacher is coming | Make friends cross | Stop friends talking | *Help friends feel close
exam: Which sentence describes a handshake? | One person waving a flag | *Two people taking each other's right hand and shaking it | Two people kicking a ball | Two people clapping their own hands
